    }
    {
        key: "Ctrl+Shift+O"
        title: "Reopen a recent workspace in a new window"
        use: "Same picker as `Ctrl+Shift+S`, but it opens in a new OS window and leaves the pane you were in alone."
        topic: "containers"
        task: "containers"
        step: 3
        does: "recent-workspace"
        mode: "terminal"
        also: ["Ctrl+Shift+S"]
        why: "A window, not a tab, and that is the point: there are no tabs. This key replaced `Ctrl+Shift+T`, which was documented as an open collision — it was the terminal's own new-tab default AND the tab reconciler's manual path, so the drift check passed off the default alone whether or not a capsule binding was ever written. Both of those are gone, and the collision went with them. The picker runs the shell directly rather than attaching to the session, because it is a one-shot that should exit with itself."
        verify: [{kind: "wezterm-key", key: "O", mods: "CTRL"}]
